%% D13: Team Init Wizard (v5)
%% oh team init: join or create the team-state repository, then 4 adaptive
%% steps. --solo creates a local team-state without remote (workflow space
%% of a project without a team), promotable later with oh team promote.

flowchart TD
    Start([oh team init]) --> Q{--solo?}

    Q -- No --> S0[Team-state repository<br/>created beforehand on GitLab/GitHub]
    S0 --> S1[1. Global config<br/>takeover, sessions]
    S1 --> S2[2. Identity<br/>member registration]
    S2 --> S3[3. Notifications<br/>Mattermost, optional]
    S3 --> S4[4. Team policies<br/>automated conventions]
    S4 --> Done([Team ready])

    Q -- Yes --> SO[Solo space<br/>~/.oh/teams/&lt;id&gt;/ · git init, no remote<br/>single member, lead]
    SO --> SP[Optional: attach a project<br/>--project &lt;p&gt;]
    SP --> SDone([Solo space ready])
    SDone -.->|"oh team promote --remote &lt;url&gt;"| Done

    Done --> Artefacts
    SDone --> Artefacts

    subgraph Artefacts["team-state repository"]
        A1[config.toml · members.toml · policies.toml]
        A2[workflows/ published · drafts · prompts · history<br/>workflows.lock]
        A3[catalog/ agents · skills]
        A4[projects/ · wiki/ · reports/]
    end

    style Start fill:#4a90d9,color:#fff
    style Done fill:#2ecc71,color:#fff
    style SDone fill:#2ecc71,color:#fff
    style Artefacts fill:#f0f0f0,stroke:#ccc
